### Cathode API walk-through (run cathode-host --serve and cathode-server first; see engine/README.md).
### Builds a small rig, edits channels and scenes, saves it. Rider and VS Code (REST Client) run these directly.
@base = http://127.0.0.1:5180/api/v1

### Engine status
GET {{base}}/system

### Block types the editor can place
GET {{base}}/catalog/blocks

### Start from Input -> shunts -> Output
POST {{base}}/live/new

### Drop a drive on the shunt at row 0, column 1
POST {{base}}/live/blocks
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "type": "drive",
    "row": 0,
    "column": 1
}

### ...and a delay at column 2
POST {{base}}/live/blocks
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "type": "delay",
    "row": 0,
    "column": 2
}

### Channel A: light crunch (the active channel, so it is heard at once)
PATCH {{base}}/live/blocks/drive1/params
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "drive": 3,
    "tone": 6
}

### Channel B: lead drive (stored, not heard until a scene uses it)
PATCH {{base}}/live/blocks/drive1/params?channel=B
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "drive": 8,
    "tone": 7,
    "level": -3
}

### Scene 2: switch to it, put the drive on channel B, bypass the delay
PUT {{base}}/live/scenes/active
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "scene": 1
}

###
PUT {{base}}/live/blocks/drive1/channel
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "channel": "B"
}

###
PATCH {{base}}/live/scenes/1
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "name": "Lead"
}

### Back to scene 1: drive returns to channel A, the delay comes back; nothing recompiles
PUT {{base}}/live/scenes/active
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "scene": 0
}

### Upload an impulse response (content-addressed; the response's "ref" goes into a cab block)
POST {{base}}/assets?name=my-cab.wav
Content-Type: application/octet-stream

< ./my-cab.wav

### Save to the library
POST {{base}}/live/save
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "name": "Crunch and Lead"
}

### The library
GET {{base}}/presets

### Undo the last edit
POST {{base}}/live/undo
